        "original_id": "f9b6fbf8-07a8-53d7-aff2-4ee1726eaefb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: American Top-20, American Top 40, Scooby-Doo\n- People: Casey Kasem\n- Organizations: WMCW\n- Roles: disc jockey, music historian, radio personality, voice actor, actor\n- Topics: Adult Contemporary radio format\n\nFacts:\n- From 1969 to 1997, and again from 2002 to 2009, Casey Kasem voiced Norville \"Shaggy\" Rogers in the Scooby-Doo franchise.\n- From 1970 until his retirement in 2009, Casey Kasem hosted music radio countdown programs, most notably American Top 40.\n- During the 1990s, WMCW carried an Adult Contemporary format and aired Casey Kasem's American Top-20 on weekends.\n- Casey Kasem was born on April 27, 1932.\n- Casey Kasem was an American disc jockey, music historian, radio personality, voice actor, and actor.\n- Casey Kasem died on June 15, 2014.",
